# G9POS — Architecture Rules

## Device Roles
| Device | Role |
|--------|------|
| Android tablet | Primary POS — only active POS at a time |
| Android phone | Hot standby — pre-authenticated, background synced, one-tap activation |
| iPhone/laptop/browser | Remote dashboard — monitoring + staff create + device revoke + CSV catalog import |

Only one device is the active POS at any time (`devices.is_active_pos`). Switching is a deliberate owner action, never automatic.

## Write Path — Shop Data
```
User action
  → Write to local SQLite (Drift)
  → Append to sync_queue
  → Return success to UI immediately
  → Background: flush queue to POST /v1/sync/events
```
No direct REST product/sale/expense/order writes. No synchronous server calls in the sale flow.

Administrative REST (not POS shop-data CRUD): `POST /v1/setup`, `POST /v1/users`, `POST /v1/devices/{id}/revoke`, `POST /v1/catalog/import`, auth, device rename.

## Sync Architecture
- **Inventory changes:** append-only event log — `INVENTORY_SOLD`, `INVENTORY_VOIDED`, `INVENTORY_RESTOCKED`, `INVENTORY_ADJUSTED`, `INVENTORY_DAMAGED`, `INVENTORY_RETURNED`
- **Everything else:** Last-Write-Wins by `created_at` timestamp, server is tiebreaker
- **Transport:** HTTP REST — sync queue flushed when connectivity detected
- **Real-time push:** WebSocket for dashboard only — never load-bearing for POS
- **Batch size:** 50 events per request, 5MB max payload
- **Event groups:** never split across batches — group by `reference_id`; standalone events are NULL
- **Idempotency:** every event has a UUID id — server ignores duplicates
- **G1:** device sets local `rejected_at` on permanently rejected unsynced `inventory_events` rows; never hard-delete; marker never leaves the device

## Offline Operation
- Full POS functionality from local SQLite indefinitely — no internet required
- JWT cached in `flutter_secure_storage` — login works offline after first auth
- Background sync every 2 hours when connectivity available
- Staleness warnings at 4h / 24h — never block a sale

## Device Failover (Tablet → Phone)
- Phone is always pre-authenticated and background-synced
- "Set as active device" is one tap — no reconfiguration
- Both devices paired to all hardware during initial setup
- `DEVICE_ACTIVATED` event queued and sent when connectivity returns

## Backend Structure
Handler → Service → Repository (three layers, always)
- Handler: parse request, call service, return response — no business logic
- Service: business logic, validation — no HTTP, no SQL
- Repository: SQL only — no business logic, no HTTP

## Infrastructure
- Single Go monolith — no microservices
- Docker Compose: nginx + go-api + postgresql
- PostgreSQL not exposed publicly — only Go API is internet-facing
- `POST /v1/setup` must be completed before API is exposed to public internet
- Daily automated backups

## Shop Timezone
```go
const ShopTimezone = "Asia/Yangon" // UTC+6:30 — never change, never use device local time
```
All "same day" logic (especially sale void) uses server shop-day, not device clock.
